{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a87d3b379c61f539", "type": "tool_result", "content": "43180 /tmp/paper_2608.html\n<head><script>document.documentElement.classList.add('js');</script>  <title>[2608.09435v1] Listen, See and Track: Spatio-Temporal Audio-Visual Sound Event Reasoning for Omni-Modal Language Models</title>\n  <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Abstract page for arXiv paper 2608.09435v1: Listen, See and Track: Spatio-Temporal Audio-Visual Sound Event Reasoning for Omni-Modal Language Models\"><meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Listen, See and Track: Spatio-Temporal Audio-Visual Sound Event Reasoning for Omni-Modal Language Models\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"Listen, See and Track: Spatio-Temporal Audio-Visual Sound Event...\"/>\n  <script src=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/js/cite.js\" type=\"text/javascript\"></script><meta name=\"citation_title\" content=\"Listen, See and Track: Spatio-Temporal Audio-Visual Sound Event Reasoning for Omni-Modal Language Models\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Zeng, Zhi\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Zhang, Cheng\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Yang, Zesheng\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Pi, Rendong\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Wu, Jiaying\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Zhang, Di\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Ma, Zihan\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Li, Guodong\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Yang, Zhou\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Xiang, Yu\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Zheng, Yifei\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Luo, Minnan\" /><meta name=\"citation_date\" content=\"2026/08/10\" /><meta name=\"citation_online_date\" content=\"2026/08/10\" /><meta name=\"citation_pdf_url\" content=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.09435\" /><meta name=\"citation_arxiv_id\" content=\"2608.09435\" /><meta name=\"citation_abstract\" content=\"Understanding dynamic sound sources requires jointly determining what produces a sound, where the source is located, and how it moves over time. Yet existing audio-language models often represent clips as global acoustic events, while vision-language models lack the spatial audio cues needed to localize and track individual sources. To evaluate this missing capability, we introduce ST-OmniQA, a spatio-temporal audio-visual question-answering benchmark built from panoramic videos paired with synchronized first-order Ambisonics (FOA) audio of moving sound sources. It contains 40K videos and 400K question-answer pairs organized into four capability levels covering sound-event recognition, direction of arrival, source distance, motion trajectories, and temporally grounded audio-visual reasoning. Building on this benchmark, we propose ST-Omni-R1, which integrates FOA-derived semantic and trajectory representations with panoramic visual context and is trained through progressive curriculum learning and reasoning-tree reinforcement learning. ST-Omni-R1 achieves 77.83\\% average semantic accuracy across the four levels, compared with 37.28\\% for the best evaluated baseline. Results on three public spatial-audio benchmarks further indicate that its learned spatial and motion representations transfer beyond ST-OmniQA.\" />\n        placeholder=\"Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...\">\n        dc:title=\"Listen, See and Track: Spatio-Temporal Audio-Visual Sound Event Reasoning for Omni-Modal Language Models\"\n    <h1 class=\"title mathjax\"><span class=\"descriptor\">Title:</span>Listen, See and Track: Spatio-Temporal Audio-Visual Sound Event Reasoning for Omni-Modal Language Models</h1>\n    <div class=\"authors\"><span class=\"descriptor\">Authors:</span><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Zeng,+Z\" rel=\"nofollow\">Zhi Zeng</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Zhang,+C\" rel=\"nofollow\">Cheng Zhang</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Yang,+Z\" rel=\"nofollow\">Zesheng Yang</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Pi,+R\" rel=\"nofollow\">Rendong Pi</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Wu,+J\" rel=\"nofollow\">Jiaying Wu</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Zhang,+D\" rel=\"nofollow\">Di Zhang</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Ma,+Z\" rel=\"nofollow\">Zihan Ma</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Li,+G\" rel=\"nofollow\">Guodong Li</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Yang,+Z\" rel=\"nofollow\">Zhou Yang</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Xiang,+Y\" rel=\"nofollow\">Yu Xiang</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Zheng,+Y\" rel=\"nofollow\">Yifei Zheng</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Luo,+M\" rel=\"nofollow\">Minnan Luo</a></div>            <div id=\"download-button-info\" hidden>View a PDF of the paper titled Listen, See and Track: Spatio-Temporal Audio-Visual Sound Event Reasoning for Omni-Modal Language Models, by Zhi Zeng and 11 other authors</div>\n    <blockquote class=\"abstract mathjax\">\n            <span class=\"descriptor\">Abstract:</span>Understanding dynamic sound sources requires jointly determining what produces a sound, where the source is located, and how it moves over time. Yet existing audio-language models often represent clips as global acoustic events, while vision-language models lack the spatial audio cues needed to localize and track individual sources. To evaluate this missing capability, we introduce ST-OmniQA, a spatio-temporal audio-visual question-answering benchmark built from panoramic videos paired with synchronized first-order Ambisonics (FOA) audio of moving sound sources. It contains 40K videos and 400K question-answer pairs organized into four capability levels covering sound-event recognition, direction of arrival, source distance, motion trajectories, and temporally grounded audio-visual reasoning. Building on this benchmark, we propose ST-Omni-R1, which integrates FOA-derived semantic and trajectory representations with panoramic visual context and is trained through progressive curriculum learning and reasoning-tree reinforcement learning. ST-Omni-R1 achieves 77.83\\% average semantic accuracy across the four levels, compared with 37.28\\% for the best evaluated baseline. Results on three public spatial-audio benchmarks further indicate that its learned spatial and motion representations transfer beyond ST-OmniQA.\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">Subjects:</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell subjects\">\n            <span class=\"primary-subject\">Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)</span></td>\nView a PDF of the paper titled Listen, See and Track: Spatio-Temporal Audio-Visual Sound Event Reasoning for Omni-Modal Language Models, by Zhi Zeng and 11 other authors</div><li><a href=\"/pdf/2608.09435v1\" aria-describedby=\"download-button-info\" accesskey=\"f\" class=\"abs-button download-pdf\">View PDF</a></li><li><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/html/2608.09435v1\" class=\"abs-button\" id=\"latexml-download-link\">HTML (experimental)</a></li><li><a href=\"/src/2608.09435v1\" class=\"abs-button download-eprint\">TeX Source\n      <div class=\"abs-license\"><a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\" title=\"Rights to this article\" class=\"has_license\">\n         accesskey=\"p\" title=\"previous in cs.AI (accesskey p)\" rel=\"nofollow\">&lt;&nbsp;prev</a>\n         title=\"next in cs.AI (accesskey n)\"  rel=\"nofollow\">next&nbsp;&gt;</a>", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "a237b0e5-392a-4800-9e67-3f13794c4065",